---
import ReadingPage from '../layouts/ReadingPage.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<ReadingPage
  title="Terms of Use – ScoreSheetSquare"
  description="Terms for using ScoreSheetSquare's free printable score sheets and online scorekeepers, including how you may print and share the sheets."
  heading="Terms of use"
  lead={`Last updated ${site.legalUpdated}.`}
  crumb="Terms"
>
  <div class="measure prose">
    <p>
      By using ScoreSheetSquare ({site.domain}) you agree to these terms. The site is run by {site.owner}. If you have a
      question about them, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="t-lead">Using the sheets</h2>
    <p>
      You may download, print and copy the score sheets as often as you like for your own games, your family, your club, your
      school or a community event, at no cost. You may not sell the sheets, offer them for download on another website, or
      present them as your own work.
    </p>

    <h2 class="t-lead">Accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      We take care that every sheet and scoring table is right, but house rules vary and mistakes can happen. The sheets and
      the online scorekeeper are provided as they are, without any guarantee. Please check scores that matter, and tell us
      about any mistake you find.
    </p>

    <h2 class="t-lead">Games scored online</h2>
    <p>
      Games are saved only in your browser. We cannot recover a game that was cleared from your device, and we are not
      responsible for scores that are lost.
    </p>

    <h2 class="t-lead">Trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      ScoreSheetSquare is independent and not affiliated with any game publisher. Game names are trademarks of their owners
      and are used only to identify which game a sheet is for.
    </p>

    <h2 class="t-lead">Links and ads</h2>
    <p>The site shows ads and may link to other websites. We are not responsible for the content of other websites.</p>

    <h2 class="t-lead">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. The new version will be posted here with a new date, and continuing to use the site means you
      accept it.
    </p>
  </div>
</ReadingPage>

<style>
  .prose { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .prose h2 { margin-block-start: 24px; }
</style>
